<ProseLayout
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  kicker="Transparency"
  path="/affiliate-disclosure/"
  updated={new Date('2026-09-26')}
  description="ShopOwnerStack is free to read. We earn money from some links to software vendors and from display advertising. This page explains how, and what that does and does not change."
>
  <h2>Do you earn money from the links on this site?</h2>
  <p>
    Sometimes. Buttons such as "Visit Jobber" or "Try Housecall Pro" go through a link on our own
    domain (for example <code>/go/jobber/</code>) and then on to the vendor. If the vendor runs a
    partner programme and we are part of it, they may pay us a commission when you sign up or
    request a demo. You never pay more because of it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Those links are marked as sponsored for search engines, and every page that contains them
    carries a short disclosure near the first link.
  </p>

  <h2>Do you show ads?</h2>
  <p>
    We may show display advertising served by Google AdSense or a similar network. Ads are clearly
    labelled "Advertisement" and are chosen by the ad network, not by us. An advertiser cannot buy
    a review, a rating or a position in a list.
  </p>

  <h2>Does it change ratings or rankings?</h2>
  <p>
    No. Ratings come from the published rubric on <a href="/how-we-test/">how we review</a>. Lists
    are ordered by those ratings automatically. A product with no partner programme is reviewed,
    rated and ranked exactly like one with a generous commission, and several of the products we
    cover pay us nothing.
  </p>

  <h2>Do vendors see reviews before publication?</h2>
  <p>
    No. Vendors do not get to approve, edit or pre-read reviews. If a vendor points out a factual
    error, we check it against a public source and correct it if they are right, as we would for
    any reader.
  </p>

  <h2>Why disclose any of this?</h2>
  <p>
    Because you should know how a site that recommends products gets paid, and because the US
    Federal Trade Commission's Endorsement Guides require clear disclosure of material connections.
    If anything here is unclear, <a href="/contact/">ask us</a>.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
